  "articleBodyHtml": "<h2>Speaker&#x27;s Lack of Control Over Actions</h2>\n<p>The speaker is unable to control their actions, as indicated by repeated statements such as &#x27;I can&#x27;t help it.&#x27; This suggests a sense of helplessness or lack of agency in the situation.</p>\n<h2>Desire to Enter the Refrigerator</h2>\n<p>The speaker expresses a strong desire to enter the refrigerator, as seen in the statement &#x27;I really want to go in.&#x27; This indicates a specific intention or need related to the refrigerator.</p>\n<h2>Location at a Convenience Store</h2>\n<p>The speaker is located at a convenience store, as repeatedly stated in &#x27;To the convenience store.&#x27; This confirms the location context of the speaker.</p>\n<h2>Poor Situation</h2>\n<p>The situation is described as not being good, as indicated by the statement &#x27;This isn&#x27;t good either.&#x27; This suggests a negative or problematic context.</p>\n<h2>Agreement with a Statement</h2>\n<p>The speaker agrees with a previous statement, as seen in &#x27;See?&#x27; This indicates a form of acknowledgment or agreement.</p>\n<h2>Alcohol Consumption</h2>\n<p>The speaker mentions that the person in question consumes alcohol, as stated in &#x27;He has alcohol too.&#x27; This provides information about the individual&#x27;s habits.</p>\n<h2>Affirmation of a Statement</h2>\n<p>The speaker affirms a previous statement, as seen in &#x27;It is.&#x27; This indicates agreement or confirmation.</p>\n<h2>Uniqueness of a Person</h2>\n<p>The speaker states that there is no one like the person in question, as indicated by &#x27;There&#x27;s no one like him.&#x27; This highlights the individual&#x27;s uniqueness.</p>\n<h2>Real Builder</h2>\n<p>The speaker refers to the person as a real builder, as stated in &#x27;He is the realbuilder.&#x27; This suggests recognition of the individual&#x27;s authenticity or skill.</p>\n<h2>Amazement at Someone</h2>\n<p>The speaker expresses amazement at the person, as seen in &#x27;He&#x27;s amazing too.&#x27; This indicates admiration or surprise.</p>\n<h2>Kids&#x27; Game</h2>\n<p>The speaker suggests that the situation will become a kids&#x27; game, as indicated by &#x27;It will be a kids&#x27; game.&#x27; This implies a shift in context or activity.</p>\n<h2>Desire for Others to Listen to a Song</h2>\n<p>The speaker wants others to listen to a song, as stated in &#x27;I want you to listen to it.&#x27; This indicates a desire for sharing or appreciation.</p>\n<h2>Praise for a Song</h2>\n<p>The speaker praises the song as being really awesome, as seen in &#x27;And this is really awesome.&#x27; This indicates admiration for the music.</p>\n<h2>Call to Attention</h2>\n<p>The speaker calls for attention, as indicated by &#x27;Look.&#x27; This suggests a desire to draw focus or notice.</p>\n<h2>Song by Maoi the Mission</h2>\n<p>The speaker mentions a song by Maoi the Mission, as stated in &#x27;With Maoi the Mission&#x27;s.&#x27; This identifies the artist or group associated with the song.</p>\n<h2>Song Created by Others</h2>\n<p>The speaker refers to a song created by others, as seen in &#x27;I made a really good song.&#x27; This indicates the origin or creation of the song.</p>\n<h2>Desire for Everyone to Listen</h2>\n<p>The speaker wants everyone to listen to the song, as indicated by &#x27;I want everyone to listen to it.&#x27; This shows a desire for widespread appreciation or sharing.</p>\n<h2>Song Title: Don&#x27;t Lie</h2>\n<p>The speaker mentions the song title &#x27;Don&#x27;t Lie,&#x27; as stated in &#x27;It&#x27;s a song called Don&#x27;t Lie.&#x27; This identifies the specific song being referred to.</p>\n<h2>Praise for the Song</h2>\n<p>The speaker praises the song again, as seen in &#x27;It&#x27;s really awesome.&#x27; This reinforces the admiration for the music.</p>\n<h2>Happiness of Hinata</h2>\n<p>Hinata appears to be very happy, as indicated by the repeated statement &#x27;I&#x27;m so happy.&#x27; This suggests a positive emotional state.</p>\n<h2>Happiest Day of the Year</h2>\n<p>The day is described as probably the happiest of the year, as seen in &#x27;It was probably the happiest day of the year.&#x27; This highlights the significance of the event.</p>\n<h2>Shyness and Uncertainty</h2>\n<p>The speaker is shy and uncertain about their abilities, as indicated by &#x27;I can&#x27;t help it, but I&#x27;ll do my best from now on.&#x27; This suggests a lack of confidence or self-doubt.</p>\n<h2>Value of Having a Job</h2>\n<p>The speaker believes having a job is a good thing, as stated in &#x27;It&#x27;s a good thing to have a job. It&#x27;s a good thing, isn&#x27;t it?&#x27; This indicates a positive view of employment.</p>\n<h2>Gratitude to Calliope</h2>\n<p>The speaker expresses gratitude to Calliope, as seen in &#x27;I&#x27;m really grateful.&#x27; This indicates appreciation or thanks.</p>\n<h2>Gratitude to Calliope for a Specific Action</h2>\n<p>The speaker is grateful to Calliope for a specific action, as indicated by &#x27;I&#x27;m really grateful to Calliope for that.&#x27; This shows appreciation for a particular contribution.</p>\n<h2>Surprise at Japanese Fans</h2>\n<p>The speaker is surprised by the presence of Japanese fans, as stated in &#x27;I can&#x27;t believe there are Japanese fans. I can&#x27;t believe there are Japanese fans.&#x27; This indicates astonishment or disbelief.</p>\n<h2>Gratitude for Attendance</h2>\n<p>The speaker is grateful for the attendance of others, as seen in &#x27;See?&#x27; This suggests appreciation for the presence or support of others.</p>\n<h2>記事情報</h2>\n<p>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gSqt3LiytVI</p>",
